Disable [[clang::musttail]] in skcms when not compiling with Clang.

GCC 15 reports support for the clang::musttail attribute, so skcms enables it,
but on RISC-V (lp64d) GCC cannot always emit the required tail call and fails with
"error: cannot tail-call: tail call production failed" in skcms_TransformBaseline.cc.
Falling back to the non-musttail code path (SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL=0) avoids the error.

--- a/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h
+++ b/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h
@@ -59,3 +59,3 @@
     #elif !defined(__clang__) && !defined(SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL)
         #if __has_cpp_attribute(clang::musttail)
-            #define SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL 1
+            #define SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL 0
